# One identity per person, however git happened to be configured that day.
#
# This file only changes what git *reports* - `git shortlog -sne`, `git blame`,
# `git log --use-mailmap`, and the contributor list GitHub renders. It rewrites
# no history and no commit object.
#
# What put a person here: a personal address that later became a work address
# splits the same contributor into two rows for no reason anyone would want.
# A laptop with no `user.email` set does the same thing per machine, signing as
# `<user>@<hostname>.local`, which is not an address at all.
#
# Left of the second `<...>` is the canonical identity; right of it is the
# spelling found in history. Add a line rather than asking anyone to rewrite a
# commit.
#
# Format: Proper Name <proper@email> <commit@email>
# See `git help shortlog` (MAPPING AUTHORS).

Griffin <griffin@billylives.com> <griffin@billylives.com>
